{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00488",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 1.22,
      "end_seconds": 6.15,
      "duration_seconds": 4.93,
      "text": "Um, morning. Nice to finally see you, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 7.29,
      "end_seconds": 12.47,
      "duration_seconds": 5.18,
      "text": "Of course, put it down anywhere. So, how can I help?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 14.01,
      "end_seconds": 17.49,
      "duration_seconds": 3.48,
      "text": "Doctor, thank you for seeing us."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 19.35,
      "end_seconds": 21.94,
      "duration_seconds": 2.59,
      "text": "Absolutely, come and sit beside them."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 22.64,
      "end_seconds": 33.67,
      "duration_seconds": 11.03,
      "text": "Well, I've been having pain in my lower back. I just want to get back to normal, really."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 35.13,
      "end_seconds": 40.19,
      "duration_seconds": 5.06,
      "text": "How long are we talking about? Take your time, there's no rush."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 44.74,
      "end_seconds": 57.44,
      "duration_seconds": 12.7,
      "text": "For one week, I'd say. I thought it would sort itself out, but it hasn't. I'm not great at remembering details, so bear with me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 58.43,
      "end_seconds": 67.78,
      "duration_seconds": 9.35,
      "text": "Tell me a bit more about it: how bad it gets, how often, and whether anything makes it better or worse."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 69.32,
      "end_seconds": 88.09,
      "duration_seconds": 18.77,
      "text": "Okay, so I'd give it a six, out of ten. Sitting for long definitely sets it off. Hmm, and there's pain going into the buttock as well, about a month now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 89.08,
      "end_seconds": 91.13,
      "duration_seconds": 2.05,
      "text": "How intense does it get?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 93.22,
      "end_seconds": 103.29,
      "duration_seconds": 10.07,
      "text": "Well, you know, I'd give it a four, out of ten. There was stiffness, yes, but that went away."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 104.53,
      "end_seconds": 110.99,
      "duration_seconds": 6.46,
      "text": "So, a few quick ones: weakness in the legs, weight loss, fever or bladder problems?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 112.89,
      "end_seconds": 120.2,
      "duration_seconds": 7.31,
      "text": "I haven't had weakness in the legs, weight loss, fever or bladder problems, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 121.86,
      "end_seconds": 124.74,
      "duration_seconds": 2.88,
      "text": "Nothing like numbness in the legs?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 125.9,
      "end_seconds": 129.26,
      "duration_seconds": 3.36,
      "text": "Nope, no numbness in the legs."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 131.18,
      "end_seconds": 134.86,
      "duration_seconds": 3.68,
      "text": "Anything with your heart, like skipped beats or fainting?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 135.76,
      "end_seconds": 137.5,
      "duration_seconds": 1.74,
      "text": "Nothing like that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 155.94,
      "end_seconds": 159.2,
      "duration_seconds": 3.26,
      "text": "What medicines are you taking at the moment?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 160.5,
      "end_seconds": 171.9,
      "duration_seconds": 11.4,
      "text": "Ramipril. I take it 5 milligrams, every morning for my blood pressure. Diclofenac. I take it 50 milligrams, when needed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 173.8,
      "end_seconds": 182.28,
      "duration_seconds": 8.48,
      "text": "It's meant to be when needed, though I don't see he take it every time."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 184.79,
      "end_seconds": 193.7,
      "duration_seconds": 8.91,
      "text": "I'm on paracetamol, 500 milligrams, when needed. I did try to ignore it for a while."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 194.89,
      "end_seconds": 196.07,
      "duration_seconds": 1.18,
      "text": "Is that long-standing?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 197.69,
      "end_seconds": 199.91,
      "duration_seconds": 2.22,
      "text": "About a month now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 201.11,
      "end_seconds": 206.41,
      "duration_seconds": 5.3,
      "text": "What about your general health, any conditions you're being treated for?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 208.41,
      "end_seconds": 218.68,
      "duration_seconds": 10.27,
      "text": "Um, I've had high blood pressure, yes. I have arthritis in my knees, for five years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 219.69,
      "end_seconds": 226.96,
      "duration_seconds": 7.27,
      "text": "Right, so arthritis in your knees is already on your record. We'll keep that in mind today."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 237.61,
      "end_seconds": 240.19,
      "duration_seconds": 2.58,
      "text": "Have you had any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 241.74,
      "end_seconds": 245.77,
      "duration_seconds": 4.03,
      "text": "Hmm, no, never had any surgery."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 246.74,
      "end_seconds": 251.66,
      "duration_seconds": 4.92,
      "text": "Do you have any allergies to medicines, food, anything at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 253.37,
      "end_seconds": 256.1,
      "duration_seconds": 2.73,
      "text": "No, no allergies to anything."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 257.16,
      "end_seconds": 266.08,
      "duration_seconds": 8.92,
      "text": "Hold on, doctor, I think he reacted to sulfa drugs once. I'm not certain, though."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 267.6,
      "end_seconds": 270.18,
      "duration_seconds": 2.58,
      "text": "So, I don't remember that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 272.26,
      "end_seconds": 280.65,
      "duration_seconds": 8.39,
      "text": "Alright, so that's unclear. I'll record what each of you said. Do your parents or siblings have any long-term illnesses?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 282.11,
      "end_seconds": 286.47,
      "duration_seconds": 4.36,
      "text": "Okay, so my father had a stroke."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 287.66,
      "end_seconds": 289.5,
      "duration_seconds": 1.84,
      "text": "And alcohol, how much?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 290.47,
      "end_seconds": 295.33,
      "duration_seconds": 4.86,
      "text": "A beer or two most evenings, to be honest."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 296.19,
      "end_seconds": 297.45,
      "duration_seconds": 1.26,
      "text": "How about smoking?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 298.69,
      "end_seconds": 302.93,
      "duration_seconds": 4.24,
      "text": "I smoke, yes, around five a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 304.15,
      "end_seconds": 305.45,
      "duration_seconds": 1.3,
      "text": "And your work?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 306.05,
      "end_seconds": 309.78,
      "duration_seconds": 3.73,
      "text": "I drive a delivery van all day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 311.81,
      "end_seconds": 313.95,
      "duration_seconds": 2.14,
      "text": "Who's at home with you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 314.47,
      "end_seconds": 319.12,
      "duration_seconds": 4.65,
      "text": "It's just me and my wife at home now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 320.13,
      "end_seconds": 322.86,
      "duration_seconds": 2.73,
      "text": "Let me check your vitals now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 332.33,
      "end_seconds": 334.49,
      "duration_seconds": 2.16,
      "text": "Okay, give me a moment..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 352.73,
      "end_seconds": 364.04,
      "duration_seconds": 11.31,
      "text": "Okay: BP is 115 over 82, weight 57 kilos. And temperature is 37.0 degrees, saturation 99 percent, height 186 centimetres, heart rate 77."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 366.26,
      "end_seconds": 368.83,
      "duration_seconds": 2.57,
      "text": "I'd like to examine you now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 369.76,
      "end_seconds": 371.71,
      "duration_seconds": 1.95,
      "text": "Bear with me a second."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 383.81,
      "end_seconds": 389.91,
      "duration_seconds": 6.1,
      "text": "Straight leg raise is negative on both sides and power in the legs is normal."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 391.77,
      "end_seconds": 393.73,
      "duration_seconds": 1.96,
      "text": "Tell me if anything hurts."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 402.46,
      "end_seconds": 407.18,
      "duration_seconds": 4.72,
      "text": "There's tenderness over the muscles on the right of the lower back."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 410.64,
      "end_seconds": 412.8,
      "duration_seconds": 2.16,
      "text": "Okay, you can sit up."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 425.16,
      "end_seconds": 454.5,
      "duration_seconds": 29.34,
      "text": "So where does that leave us? The most likely explanation is mechanical low back pain. I'd also keep a disc problem in mind. Staying gently active heals back pain faster than bed rest, so keep moving. One warning sign to remember: you get numbness in the groin or lose bladder control. In that case don't wait. Is there anything you wanted to ask?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 455.99,
      "end_seconds": 459.67,
      "duration_seconds": 3.68,
      "text": "Uh, I appreciate it, doctor."
    }
  ]
}